{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "id": "domashniy-arest-s01e01-scene-27",
 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Новый мэр  (The New Mayor)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "arkady": "Аркадий",
  "samson": "Самсон"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "We stay in the shared kitchen, with the same bad vodka. Last time, Pasha announced on television that he is running for mayor, and Samson told Arkady that all officials are thieves and nobody cares. Suddenly Arkady looks at Samson in a new way. We'll hear it in Russian first; don't worry about catching every word.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Как я сразу не догадался!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Самсон, ты русский?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Нет, эфиоп!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Не сидел?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Нет, слава богу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Православный?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ну а какой?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Русский. Православный. Не сидел.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ну да. Жена, двое детей.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Работал на стройке. Служил?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Служил, конечно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Вот оно! Самсон, ты будешь новым мэром.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Согласен.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Ты не понял меня. Я тебя сделаю новым мэром.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Меня? Мэром?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Через два месяца выборы. Ты же хотел новый уровень.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ну, хотел.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Я помогу тебе, а ты поможешь мне.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's take it slowly. Arkady has just had an idea, and he is cross with himself for not having it sooner.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Как я сразу не догадался!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Why didn't I think of it right away!' Literally, 'how did I not guess at once'. The action word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "догадался!",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is in the past for a male, with no extra ending, matching Arkady's gender. Then he starts asking strange questions.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Самсон, ты русский?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Samson, are you Russian?' the expression for Russian is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "русский?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " A question in Russian is often just a statement with a rising voice. Samson answers with a joke.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Нет, эфиоп!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, Ethiopian!' the expression meaning an ethiopian is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "эфиоп!",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " A big, blond, very Russian man, being sarcastic. Arkady ignores it and goes on down his list.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Не сидел?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Never been in prison?' Literally, 'didn't sit?' In everyday speech, the action word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "сидел?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'did time'. Samson is glad to say no.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Нет, слава богу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, thank God.' The phrase translates to 'glory to God', built from the term for glory, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "слава",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ". Next question.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Православный?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Orthodox?' meaning Orthodox is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Православный?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " He means the Orthodox church, the main church in Russia. Samson finds the question silly.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ну а какой?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well, what else?' The describing word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "какой?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to 'which one', as if there could be no other answer. Arkady sums it up.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Русский. Православный. Не сидел.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Russian. Orthodox. Never been in prison.' Three ticks on an invisible form. Samson adds his family.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ну да. Жена, двое детей.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well, yes. A wife, two kids.' After meaning two, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "двое",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the translation for children, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "детей.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", takes a special form, one you hear a lot. Arkady continues.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Работал на стройке. Служил?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Worked on a building site. Did you serve in the army?' Again, past action words like ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Служил?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " have no subject: the ending tells you it's a man. Samson is proud of this one.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Служил, конечно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Of course I served.' He repeats the key action word for served, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Служил,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " as his answer, which is a common way to say yes. And Arkady has his candidate.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Вот оно! Самсон, ты будешь новым мэром.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'That's it! Samson, you're going to be the new mayor.' After the action word for 'to be', ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "будешь",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the job takes a special ending for roles: you'll be 'as mayor', ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "мэром.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " Samson thinks it's just drunken talk.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Согласен.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Agreed.' the Russian word translates to agreed, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Согласен.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " Said like a man accepting another glass. Arkady insists.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Ты не понял меня. Я тебя сделаю новым мэром.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You don't understand me. I'm going to make you the new mayor.' the Russian for mayor, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "мэром.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", takes the same special ending for roles. Now Samson listens.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Меня? Мэром?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Me? Mayor?' the Russian for mayor here is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Мэром?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " Two short questions, and he can hardly believe it. Arkady explains the plan.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Через два месяца выборы. Ты же хотел новый уровень.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The election is in two months. You wanted a new level, didn't you?' The little word for 'didn't you' or 'after all', ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "же",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", reminds Samson of his own words. Samson admits it.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ну, хотел.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well, I did.' Just the action word for wanted again, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "хотел.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", in the past. And Arkady offers the deal.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Я помогу тебе, а ты поможешь мне.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I'll help you, and you'll help me.' Both action words are about the future. Two forms of the term for help, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "помогу",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " for 'I', and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "поможешь",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " for 'you', a neat pair to remember. Here is the whole scene one more time.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Как я сразу не догадался!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Самсон, ты русский?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
